#
# Scenario 1: normal boot, topology available - the socket
# distribution line's per-socket counts must sum to
# @@innodb_buffer_pool_instances, whatever this host's actual
# socket count is.
#
# restart: --innodb-buffer-pool-instances=8 --innodb-buffer-pool-size=128M
include/wait_for_pattern_in_file.inc [buffer pool instances per socket]
PASS: per-socket instance counts sum to the actual instance count
#
# Scenario 2: topology forced unavailable (debug point) - every
# instance falls back to the pre-patch single-CPU formula, and the
# distribution summary must not appear anywhere in the log written
# since this restart (only the portion after the byte offset
# recorded just before restarting is checked, since scenario 1's
# own distribution line is still in the same cumulative error log
# file).
#
# restart: --debug=d,bp_socket_cpuset_unavailable --innodb-buffer-pool-instances=4 --innodb-buffer-pool-size=128M
include/wait_for_pattern_in_file.inc [Buffer pool initialization completed]
PASS: fallback path completed init and printed no socket distribution line
# restart:
